[\\n\\t\\t\\\"// classname \\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for main class | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Main\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_main\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// main fnc to run the code.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for main fnc | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment sc obj\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_sc\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// creating sc object of Scanner class for taking input or running input fncs.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Scanner object | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\\"Comment Switch end\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_switchend\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// switch case ends here.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Switch case ending | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\\"Comment Main fnc end\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_mainend\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// main fnc closes here.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for main fnc ending | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\\"Comment class end\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_classend\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// class ends here.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for class ending | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\\"Comment sc obj close\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_close\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// closing the obj of Scanner class so no further input could be taken; Not Necessary.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Scanner obj closing | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment printf\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_format\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// using system.out.printf() or .format(), to print the strings and variable combined more easily.\\\\n// The syntax is like this- (\\\\\\\"String part %d %s %f %c\\\\\\\" , variables), \\\\n// In this all characters followed by % sign represent data type of variables like %s - String, %c - char %f - float, %d - integer.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Scanner obj closing | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Math random\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_random\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// uses Math.random() to generate a random number between 0.1 - 1.0\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Math.random() fnc | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Array\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_array\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// A array variable arr[] of length 5 and type double, only declared not initialized.\\\\n// Array is a variable which can store more than 1 data.\\\\n// Array Syntax:-  <datatype> <arrayname>[] = new <datatype>[length];\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Array variable | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment while Loop Ends\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_while\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// While Loop Ends here.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for while loop ending | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Array Length\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_length\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// here .length is a fnc provided by java to find the length of any array.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Array.length func | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Array Initialization\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_initArray\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// Initialization Syntax:- <arrayname> [index] = value;\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Array Initialization Syntax | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Array Initialization & Declaration\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_initDeclArray\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// Now the Time For Both Declaraton as well as initialization Syntax:-\\\\n\\\\n// <datatype> <arrayname>[] = {value1 , value2 ,value3 , ...};\\\\n\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Array Initialization & Declaration Syntax | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Array Jump Keyword\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_break\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// Uses break Keyword to exit the loop immediately without doing other iterations.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for break Keyword | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment if condition\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_if\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// if condition checking a condition, if the condition is true then if code will execute and if the condition is false nothing will execute.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for if condition | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Package name\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_package\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// package name \\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Package Name | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment boolean Data Type\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_bool\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"//Boolean datatype because it only contains either true or false as value.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Boolean Datatype | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Double Data Type\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_double\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// double dataype because it may contain decimal values.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Double Datatype | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\\"Comment Float Data Type\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_float\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// Float dataype because it may contain decimal values.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Float Datatype | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Integer Data Type\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_integer\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// Integer Datatype because it doesn't contain any floating/decimal values.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Integer Datatype | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment object creation\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_obj\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// Creating an object 'obj' of Class classname to access the class methods and variables.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Obj Declaration | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Object syntax creation\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_syntaxobj\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// Syntax of obj creation:- <classname> <objectname> = new <classname> ();\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Obj Syntax | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Custom Created Fnc\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_customfnc\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\" // A custom Created fnc 'getArgs' taking 2 parameters 'b' and 'e' of datatype double, returning void(nothing) to the Caller.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Custom Created fnc | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Custom Created Class\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_customClass\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// Custom Created Class 'CalcPower' means (doesn't contain main fnc) , classname CalcPower\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Custom Created Class | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Custom Created Class Invoking Package\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_pkginfo\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// <- use Your own Custom package name here in which you have the previous program (pg 9.16) to invoke its classes.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Custom Created Class invoking Package | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Enhanced for loop on Arrays\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_forarray\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// For loop created and variable k of same data type of array iterating on each value of array.\\\\n\\\\n// Remember: k is not the index, it is the value of array.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Enhanced For Loop on array | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Class Variable\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_classvar\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// Class variable means defined wtihout any fnc/method, it can be accessed anywhere and in any fnc inside the Class.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Class variables | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Long Datatype\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_long\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// Long datatype because the limit of Integer datatype was 2,147,483,647 . So using long datatype whose limit is 9,223,372,036,854,775,807.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Long datatype | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\n\\\"Comment Access specifier\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_private\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// private (access specifier) used here so that no other class other than this class can access this variables directly or through objects.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Private access specifier | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Setter\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_setter\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// A setter fnc 'fnc' to set the value of private variable 'var' taking 1 paramter 'r' of datatype Integer. \\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Setter fnc | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment getter\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_getter\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// A getter fnc 'GetRadius()' to get the value of private variable 'radius' in form of returned value(double) from the fnc, taking no paramters. \\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for getter fnc | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Function calling from object\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_objfnc\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// Accessing setter fnc 'SetRadius(r)' of the custom class 'Circle' using the object 'shape'.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for calling fnc from object | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Constructor Fnc\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_constructor\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// A Constructor fnc 'Employee()' returning nothing, taking no parameters.\\\\n\\\\n// this is the constructor fnc of 0 parameters.\\\\n\\\\n// A constructor fnc is the fnc with the same name of the class, and which can be called directly during object creation or just by new keyword.\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Constructor fnc | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment overloaded Fnc\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_overloaded\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// Overloaded functions are the functions which have the same name but taking diffrent no. of parameters inside them.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for overloaded fnc | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Parent class\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_parent\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\" // This class is the parent class, means it doesnt inherit anything of any other class but other classes or derived classes can access this class through extends keyword.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Parent class | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment extends keyword\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_extends\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// Using 'extends' keyword, It Extends or inherit the data members(variables and methods) of parent class 'Parent_Class'.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for extends keyword | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Parent obj Inheritance of Variables\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_parentvar\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// Accessing the variable 'var' of the custom class 'Parent_class' using the object 'derived' of 'Child_class' bacause 'Child_class' extends 'Parent_class' and it has access to all the variables and methods of 'Parent_class'.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Parent variable accesing through child obj | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n\\\"Comment Parent obj Inheritance Of Methods\\\": {\\n\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"c_parentmethod\\\",\\n\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\\"// Accessing the custom fnc 'func()' of the custom class 'Parent_class' using the object 'derived' of 'Child_class' bacause 'Child_class' extends 'Parent_class' and it has access to all the variables and methods of 'Parent_class'.\\\"\\n\\t],\\n\\t\\\"description\\\": \\\"java short desciption comment for Parent Method accessing through Child object | Code Manufactured By DHDK\\\"\\n// }\\n},\\n\\n}\",\"javascript.json\":\"{\\n\\t// Place your snippets for javascript here. Each snippet is defined under a snippet name and has a prefix, body and \\n\\t// description. The prefix is what is used to trigger the snippet and the body will be expanded and inserted. Possible variables are:\\n\\t// $1, $2 for tab stops, $0 for the final cursor position, and ${1:label}, ${2:another} for placeholders. Placeholders with the \\n\\t\\\"React Boilerplate\\\":{\\n\\t\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"rafce\\\",\\n\\t\\t\\\"body\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"use client\\\\\\\"\\\\nimport React, { useState } from \\\\\\\"react\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\nconst Page = () => {\\\\nreturn(\\\\n<>\\\\n</>\\\\n);\\\\n};\\\\nexport default Page;\\\"\\n\\t}\\n}\",\"MySnippet.code-snippets\":\"{\\n\\t// Place your global snippets here. Each snippet is defined under a snippet name and has a scope, prefix, body and \\n\\t// description. Add comma separated ids of the languages where the snippet is applicable in the scope field. If scope \\n\\t// is left empty or omitted, the snippet gets applied to all languages. The prefix is what is \\n\\t// used to trigger the snippet and the body will be expanded and inserted. Possible variables are: \\n\\t// $1, $2 for tab stops, $0 for the final cursor position, and ${1:label}, ${2:another} for placeholders. \\n\\t// Placeholders with the same ids are connected.\\n\\t// Example:\\n\\t\\\"Cdn\\\": {\\n\\t\\t\\\"scope\\\": \\\"javascript,typescript,html\\\",\\n\\t\\t\\\"prefix\\\": \\\"CDN\\\",\\n\\t\\t\\\"body\\\": [\\n\\t\\t\\t\\\"<script src=\\\\\\\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/locomotive-scroll@3.5.4/dist/locomotive-scroll.js\\\\\\\"></script>\\\\n<script src=\\\\\\\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.1/gsap.min.js\\\\\\\" integrity=\\\\\\\"sha512-qF6akR/fsZAB4Co1QDDnUXWnaQseLGXoniuSuSlPQK6+aWhlMZcHzkasCSlnWoe+TJuudlka1/IQ01Dnhgq95g==\\\\\\\" crossorigin=\\\\\\\"anonymous\\\\\\\" referrerpolicy=\\\\\\\"no-referrer\\\\\\\"